# Rebound demo chart.
#
# Deliberately sparse. This is the chart used to check that the game works, not
# to show off what it can do, so everything in it is meant to be watched rather
# than survived: quarter notes at 150 BPM, one idea at a time, and a clear gap
# after every gold object so the rally it sets off can actually be followed
# across the field.
#
# Four rows to a measure, so one row is a quarter note (400 ms).
#
# A column decides nothing for bar objects -- they land at random positions -- so
# the only columns that matter are the ones green objects sit in, which pick
# which of the three tap points they arrive at: 1 is left, 7 centre, 14 right.
# Distinct columns are still used for simultaneous objects, to keep them apart.
#
#   0 nothing   1 tap   2 gold   3 long start   4 long end   5 green   6 chain
#   7 tap  8 gold  9 chain  G green  -- the 7/8/9/G forms mark a gold's landing.
#   [ chain start   ] chain stop   { green long start   } green long end
#
# A gold with nothing marked for it picks the next tap, gold, green or first
# chain link on its own; the 7/8/9/G forms only pin that choice down.
#
# A chain is spelled out by hand: [ opens a run, ] closes it, 6 is a middle
# link, and a gold between them joins as a member. Everything from [ to the
# next ] in the same column is one chain, and every link of a run lands on one
# spot. Two separate runs may land far apart.

title=Rebound Demo
artist=Rebound
audio=demo.wav
bpm=150
offset=0
columns=16
level=3
difficulty=NORMAL
